<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="084" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Author canonical secret-catalog manifest + generator (single source generates seeder + Configure + tokens.md + Bicep KV secret set)</title>
    <phase>H KV Federation Full Remediation</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Task tags include 'auth','azure-deployment'; introduces single-source-of-truth for KV secrets governing every customer environment; a bug here creates 4-way drift across seeder/Configure/tokens.md/Bicep. FR-36 acceptance scope.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Manifest generator authored per project CLAUDE.md model-tier defaults (Opus/Fable for Phase H canonical secret-catalog manifest generator); requires reasoning across seeder script + Configure script + tokens.md + Bicep to design a single YAML schema that fans out cleanly to all 4. High-blast-radius.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>018, 019, 020</deps>
    <tags>auth, azure-deployment, dataverse</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-12 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Author the canonical secret-catalog manifest at scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml + a PowerShell generator that fans out to produce: (a) the seeder PS script; (b) the Configure script; (c) the tokens.md documentation; (d) the Bicep KV secret set. This is r3 KV federation design Phase 3b delivery per spec.md FR-36 + owner directive #3. Manifest is the SINGLE source of truth for KV secret naming, purpose, rotation cadence, and consumers.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in YAML schema design, PowerShell code-generation patterns, Bicep secret-set syntax, and the r3 KV federation Phase 3a assessment (task 017). Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>Files scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml + scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 exist; generator produces 4 output artifacts (seeder PS, Configure script, tokens.md, Bicep KV secret set) that are byte-identical for equivalent manifest inputs (deterministic); generator supports --dry-run + --verify (compares generated vs on-disk to detect drift). Manifest enumerates every KV secret with canonical name + purpose + consumers + rotation cadence.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Per spec.md FR-36 + owner directive #3 + r3 task 017 KV federation assessment: today 4 outputs (seeder, Configure, tokens doc, Bicep) are each hand-maintained → drift. Already 3 AI-Search-key aliases across 3 casings + 6 orphan template references per §7.9 rename map. The manifest closes this by generating all 4 from ONE declarative source. r3 delivered Phase 3a assessment; r1 Phase H delivers 3b.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml</file>
      <file role="new">scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1</file>
      <file role="new">scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/generated/ (output dir)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/architecture/AZURE-RESOURCE-NAMING-CONVENTION.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/r3-handoff.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="018" status="pending">Phase G canonical KV secret names baked into Bicep</dependency>
      <dependency task="019" status="pending">Phase G vault-name param</dependency>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">Phase G spaarke-spekvcert DO-NOT-RENAME dev exception codified</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-36">SCOPE: Manifest is single-source-of-truth for KV secrets; generator produces 4 output artifacts (seeder, Configure, tokens.md, Bicep) that are byte-identical across runs (deterministic ordering).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §7.9 BINDING pre-check">SCOPE: Manifest MUST include a `never-delete` flag for Dataverse-ClientSecret and BFF-API-ClientSecret; generator refuses to omit them from any output.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §7.9">SCOPE: Manifest MUST include the spaarke-spekvcert DO-NOT-RENAME dev exception + rationale.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: Manifest schema per secret: canonical-name, purpose, consumers, rotation-cadence, never-delete, exception-note, aliases (grandfathered).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: Generator supports --dry-run (prints planned outputs without writing) + --verify (compares generated vs on-disk; exits non-zero on mismatch) — enables CI drift detection.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: Do NOT edit Bicep secret sets directly in this task — generator OWNS those outputs going forward. Task 086 owns the IaC alignment.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§11">SCOPE: NEW-surface task — justification field completed per §11 three-question gate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§10">SCOPE: Generator output includes BFF app-setting keys (canonical `__` convention); coordinates with §10 constraints on config surface.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Canonical secret-catalog manifest + code generation for 4 output artifacts</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/architecture/AZURE-RESOURCE-NAMING-CONVENTION.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/config.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Existing seeder scripts" location="scripts/">Reference for current seeder shape; generator produces the same shape from manifest.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Bicep secret-set" location="infrastructure/bicep/modules/key-vault.bicep">Reference for the Bicep secret-set output shape.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Load spec.md FR-36 + r3 task 017 assessment + docs/architecture/AZURE-RESOURCE-NAMING-CONVENTION.md.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Inventory">Enumerate every KV secret today (across seeder, Configure, tokens.md, Bicep); build the initial manifest entry per secret.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Schema">Design manifest.yaml schema: canonical-name + purpose + consumers + rotation-cadence + never-delete + exception-note + aliases.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Write manifest">Author scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml with every secret enumerated. Verify Dataverse-ClientSecret + BFF-API-ClientSecret carry never-delete=true. Verify spaarke-spekvcert carries exception-note.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Generator">Author scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1: (a) parses manifest.yaml; (b) generates seeder PS, Configure script, tokens.md, Bicep secret set into scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/generated/; (c) --dry-run mode; (d) --verify mode.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Determinism">Ensure output ordering is deterministic (alphabetical per canonical-name); two runs of the same manifest produce byte-identical outputs.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Guard">Add generator startup guard: refuse to write outputs that omit never-delete secrets; refuse to rename secrets not marked in aliases.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Test dry-run">Invoke --dry-run and inspect all 4 planned outputs.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Test verify">Copy generated outputs to canonical target paths; run --verify — expect exit 0. Modify manifest slightly; re-run --verify — expect exit non-zero.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Index update">Update TASK-INDEX.md: task 084 → ✅.</step>
    <step order="10" name="Deviations">Document any deviation in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>Closest neighbors: individual seeder scripts + Configure scripts + tokens.md doc + Bicep secret set — each hand-maintained. Grep for `canonical-secret-catalog` returns none.</existing>
    <extension>No — the drift is precisely that 4 outputs coexist with no authoritative source. Extending any one would perpetuate the drift; a manifest + generator is the design intent per FR-36 + r3 assessment.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the manifest, 4-way drift persists indefinitely (already caused 3 AI-Search-key aliases in 3 casings + 6 orphan template references per §7.9 rename map — spec.md § New Components table row 7 explicitly cites this failure mode). Next KV addition risks another alias entering only one output. Manifest is the single source that closes the drift.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="pwsh">Author and test PowerShell scripts</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="config">scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml</output>
    <output type="code">scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1</output>
    <output type="docs">scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/generated/ (generated artifacts)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml exists and enumerates every KV secret with canonical-name + purpose + consumers + rotation-cadence + never-delete + exception-note + aliases.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dataverse-ClientSecret + BFF-API-ClientSecret entries carry never-delete=true; spaarke-spekvcert carries exception-note documenting DO-NOT-RENAME dev exception.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 --dry-run prints all 4 planned outputs without writing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Two runs of Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 against the same manifest produce BYTE-IDENTICAL outputs (deterministic).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 --verify against synchronized outputs exits 0; against drifted outputs exits non-zero with the drift diff.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: generator refuses to omit never-delete secrets — attempting a manifest with never-delete=false on Dataverse-ClientSecret fails startup validation with clear diagnostic.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">PSScriptAnalyzer green on the generator; deterministic output verified.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reference: spec.md FR-36 + owner directive #3 + r3 task 017 assessment. Consumed by task 085 (alias collapse) + task 086 (IaC alignment).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
